    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan recommends a HOLD for JPM, and the evidence supports this balanced stance. The stock's trend structure remains intact \u2014 price sits above all rising moving averages (10 EMA $176.75, 50 SMA $166.90, 200 SMA $146.08) with a +19.03% 60-day return and strong franchise fundamentals. However, near-term exhaustion signals are clear: RSI rolled over from 80.33 to 73.03, MACD histogram contracted 51% in two days, relative volume at 0.82 fails to confirm the advance, and price was rejected at the Bollinger upper band ($182.28) on March 8, closing at $178.59 below its open. The risk-reward asymmetry (only ~2.1% upside to the band versus 6.5% downside to the 50 SMA) and the stretched 22.3% premium to the 200 SMA argue against chasing at current levels. Given the intact uptrend but deteriorating momentum and incomplete fundamental data (no income statement available), maintaining the position without adding or trimming aggressively is the appropriate action.\n\n**Entry Price**: 176.75\n\n**Stop Loss**: 166.9\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-modest; do not add aggressively until either a breakout above $182.28 on expanding volume or a pullback to the 50 SMA near $166.90.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
